#slide()[
#text(size: 30pt, weight: "bold")[Relative Frequency Calculation]
#v(40pt)
#only("1-")[- Relative frequency is the ratio of the frequency of a specific event to the total number of events. 📈]
#only("2-")[- Formula: $f_r = f/n$]
#only("3-")[- Example: If 20 out of 100 patients have a condition, the relative frequency is $20/100 = 0.2$. 🧮]
#only("1")[
#voiceover("Relative frequency is the ratio of the frequency of a specific event to the total number of events.")
]
#only("2")[
#voiceover("The formula for relative frequency is the frequency of the event divided by the total number of events.")
]
#only("3")[
#voiceover("For example, if 20 out of 100 patients have a condition, the relative frequency is 20 divided by 100, which equals 0.2.")
]
]


